jistanidiot@gmail.com wrote:
> So I've died countless times in Sokoban and in the Mines.  I'm
> wondering is it really necessary to do these two branches?

No, but they're a big help.  Sokoban is 50/50 to give you reflection,
and getting reflection and MR is basically the point at which I start
believing the character is probably ascendable.  And Sokoban is safer
than diving lower, IMO.

Going at least to minetown is a huge boon, too.  No reason to anger the
priest, you can buy protection, there's a guaranteed altar for B/U/C,
and often good equipment in the shops (reasonable chance of a wish from
a magic lamp, too).

If you get a luckstone, not much point in going past the town.  If no,
the luckstone is nice and it's another way to keep getting random
goodies without going too deep in the dungeons.



